In article <92052.015056WENDELL@MAINE.MAINE.EDU>, WENDELL@MAINE.MAINE.EDU (Wendell G. Wren) writes...
> to restore a game
>  NETHACK -U charactername -R
> not obvious, I know...  I had to ask nethack to tell me (NETHACK -?)

     To resume a saved game, just play again using the same character
name as when you saved the prior game; restoration is automatic.  The
-u switch is one way to specify what character name to use.  -R just
requests to play character class Rogue instead of Knight, Samurai, &c.
It has nothing to do with restoring a game, and has no affect if the
specified character name already has a save file, since the existing
saved char-class takes precedence over the command line.

